-- ============================================================================
-- T1 - Digital Services Act: exclusion of micro and small enterprises
-- Instrument : Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 (Digital Services Act)
--              http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2065/oj
--              Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC, Annex (SME definition)
-- Pinpoint   : DSA Art 19(1)-(2); Rec 2003/361/EC Annex Art 2(2)-(3), Art 4(2)
-- Version    : DSA OJ L 277, 27.10.2022 (original text); Rec OJ L 124, 20.5.2003
--              - NOT CHECKED. EUR-Lex was blocked from the spike environment, so the
--              text below is quoted from the author's knowledge and must be verified.
-- Evaluated  : 2026-09-23
-- Operative text (UNVERIFIED):
--   Art 19(1): This Section, with the exception of Article 24(3) thereof, shall not
--     apply to providers of online platforms that qualify as micro or small
--     enterprises as defined in Recommendation 2003/361/EC.
--     This Section, with the exception of Article 24(3) thereof, shall not apply to
--     providers of online platforms that previously qualified for the status of a
--     micro or small enterprise as defined in Recommendation 2003/361/EC during the
--     12 months following their loss of that status pursuant to Article 4(2)
--     thereof, except when they are very large online platforms in accordance with
--     Article 33.
--   Art 19(2): By derogation from paragraph 1 of this Article, this Section shall
--     apply to providers of online platforms that have been designated as very
--     large online platforms in accordance with Article 33, irrespective of whether
--     they qualify as micro or small enterprises.
--   Rec 2003/361/EC Annex Art 2(2): a small enterprise is defined as an enterprise
--     which employs fewer than 50 persons and whose annual turnover and/or annual
--     balance sheet total does not exceed EUR 10 million.
--   Annex Art 2(3): a microenterprise ... employs fewer than 10 persons and whose
--     annual turnover and/or annual balance sheet total does not exceed EUR 2 million.
-- Modelling:
--   * "This Section" is Chapter III Section 3 (Arts 19-28); Art 24(3) survives.
--   * Headcount is the GROUP headcount (linked and partner enterprises, Annex Arts
--     3 and 6), supplied as a fact. The aggregation itself is not modelled.
--   * Every micro enterprise is also small, so the small test decides.
--   * Art 4(2) (status changes only after two consecutive accounting periods) is
--     not modelled: the caller supplies whether and when status was lost.
-- ============================================================================

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT kleene
IMPORT `t5-dsa-online-platform`

§ `DSA Art 19 - micro and small enterprises`
@ref-map dsa-art19 https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2065/oj#art_19
@ref-map rec-2003-361 https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reco/2003/361/oj

DECLARE `Section 3 outcome` IS ONE OF
    `Not relevant: not an online platform`
    `Section 3 applies (Art 19(2): designated VLOP)`
    `Section 3 does not apply, except Art 24(3) (micro or small enterprise)`
    `Section 3 does not apply, except Art 24(3) (12 months after losing micro or small status)`
    `Section 3 applies`

@ref rec-2003-361 Annex Art 2(2)-(3)
GIVEN `group staff headcount`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `annual turnover`          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `annual balance sheet total` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`micro or small enterprise` MEANS
    `all of` (LIST (`less than` `group staff headcount` 50)
                   (`any of` (LIST (`at most` `annual turnover` 10000000)
                                   (`at most` `annual balance sheet total` 10000000))))

@ref dsa-art19 Art 19(1) second subparagraph
GIVEN `evaluation date`          IS A DATE
      `formerly micro or small`  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `status lost on`           IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`within 12 months of losing the status` MEANS
    `all of` (LIST `formerly micro or small`
                   (`before` `evaluation date` (`months after maybe` 12 `status lost on`)))

@export Does DSA Chapter III Section 3 (Arts 19-28) apply? Returns every outcome still possible; one item means settled.
@ref dsa-art19 Art 19(1)-(2)
GIVEN `evaluation date`                   IS A DATE           @desc ISO 8601
      `online platform`                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc result of T5; null if undetermined
      `designated as VLOP`                IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc null if unknown
      `group staff headcount`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER   @desc staff headcount including linked and partner enterprises; null if unknown
      `annual turnover`                   IS A MAYBE NUMBER   @desc EUR; null if unknown
      `annual balance sheet total`        IS A MAYBE NUMBER   @desc EUR; null if unknown
      `formerly micro or small`           IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc previously qualified as micro or small; null if unknown
      `status lost on`                    IS A MAYBE DATE     @desc date micro or small status was lost; null if unknown
GIVETH A LIST OF `Section 3 outcome`
`Section 3 outcome for` MEANS
    `possible outcomes`
        (LIST (PAIR OF (`not` `online platform`), `Not relevant: not an online platform`),
              (PAIR OF `designated as VLOP`, `Section 3 applies (Art 19(2): designated VLOP)`),
              (PAIR OF (`micro or small enterprise` `group staff headcount` `annual turnover` `annual balance sheet total`), `Section 3 does not apply, except Art 24(3) (micro or small enterprise)`),
              (PAIR OF (`within 12 months of losing the status` `evaluation date` `formerly micro or small` `status lost on`), `Section 3 does not apply, except Art 24(3) (12 months after losing micro or small status)`))
        `Section 3 applies`
